"comparison": "Both JPMorgan and Bank of America disclose a preferred 'single point of entry' resolution strategy where only the parent holding company files for bankruptcy, with the aim of keeping subsidiaries operational. JPMorgan states that in this strategy, the Parent Company enters bankruptcy and subsidiaries are recapitalized to continue operations or be divested (jpm_2024_1A_P039_S001). Similarly, Bank of America describes its preferred strategy as having only the parent holding company file for bankruptcy, with key operating subsidiaries provided sufficient capital and liquidity to continue operating or be wound down (bac_2024_1A_P030_S002, bac_2024_1A_P030_S003). Both also warn that if regulators deem the plan not credible, stricter capital or liquidity requirements or operational restrictions could be imposed (jpm_2024_1A_D021 summary, bac_2024_1A_P031_S001).",
